        "body": "Serve Robotics Inc. /DE/ describes itself as the future of sustainable, self-driving delivery, asking why a 2-pound burrito should move in a 2-ton car. The company presents its service as a low-emissions solution to the last-mile problem and says it is setting the standard for safety on and beyond the sidewalk, protecting customer data, employees, and the public. Its site names a delivery robot called Saymo, which it says delivers burritos and appears as John Mulaney's sidekick on the show \"Everybody's Live.\" The company describes itself as a pop culture icon.\n\nServe Robotics is a for-profit public company headquartered in San Carlos, California, trading under the ticker SERV. Its SEC CIK is 0001832483, and it also appears under the name SERVE ROBOTICS INC. The available facts record 281 California legal exposure entries for the company, with no individual cases listed.",
